      "side": 1,
      "message": "Android clang-tidy wrapper recognize TIDY_TIMEOUT to abort after the time limit, but return no error status. It emits a TIMEOUT message but not any regular tidy warning because clang-tidy emits warnings only after it completes all checks.\nNew timed out cases are easy to identify from our nightly builds warnings.html files and then they can be added to this tidy_timeout_srcs list.\nIf any change has a potential to speed up these cases, we can try to empty any tidy_timeout_srcs list and see if new compilations finish in time.\nYou can try this by grepping \"clang-tidy abort\" or \"clang-tidy used\" messages in \"TIDY_TIMEOUIT\u003d90 make tidy-frameworks-base_subset\" output.",
      "parentUuid": "1e0a90eb_ef14f13b",
      "revId": "b6f3d37719dad5e08a26c898f1fbd885426a03c8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
